/-!
# Closed decorated Robinson expansions

These certificates describe 312 selected context-tagged decorations. Each node has
sixteen children, interpreted as two substitutions of its Robinson parent and a compatible
four-by-four array of shade blocks. The auxiliary 376-state border invariant tracks a one-cell
halo in the canonical refinement. Its refinement and corner classification are consumed by
the arithmetic carrier construction.

## Main definitions

* `Canonical.Node`, `Canonical.Node.child`, `Canonical.seedNode`: the closed decorated system.
* `Canonical.BorderState`: a decorated node with parity and a local selected-border halo.

## Main results

* `Canonical.children_hCompatible_within` and the boundary counterparts certify refinement.
* `Canonical.BorderState.refine_admissible` preserves the concrete finite border invariant.
* `Canonical.BorderState.observations` identifies its halo with actual selected shade borders.

These certificates are consumed by canonical finite patches and their plane-tiling theorem;
they do not assert forcing or seed removal for arbitrary tilings.

## References

The node data retain `ShadedSubstitutionStateWitnesses.stateRows`, `childRows` and
`reachableNodes` from [lean-wang](https://github.com/edemaine/lean-wang/tree/64268a3),
revision `64268a3`, with reachable IDs reindexed by their source-list positions.
The border data retain `ShadedCarrierBorderHierarchyData.stateGroup0`
through `stateGroup15`, and its `refineState` rule. The mathematical background is the corrected
Robinson construction in [JeandelVanier2020]. The seam factorization and indexed border witnesses
compress these finite certificates without changing their semantic obligations.

-/

